WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.634
-I'm so happy to have you here.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.801
-"Prime Time."
"Prime Time," Deion Sanders.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.868
You don't like --
You don't like "Neon" Deion?

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.634
-No.
-You don't like "Neon" Deion?

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.801
-No! They tried to give me that
at Florida State.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:14.367
I'd already earned
"Prime Time" in high school.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.601
I dropped like 37 that night,
had two dunks back to back,

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:21.200
curl was wet, looked dry.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.734
And we were on our way home
on the bus, and my homie says,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.367
"You know what, man?
You're prime time."

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.567
I said, "You right."
So, it was birthed then.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.667
You can't give me no nickname.
I'm from the inner city.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.100
You can't just
give us a nickname.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.033
You got to earn that thing,
and I earned it -- "Prime Time."

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:37.367
-"Neon" Deion, though.
-I don't like "Neon" Deion.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.934
I don't like that.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.501
Well, what do I call you now?
Do I call you "Prime" or Coach?

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.167
-You can call me anything.
You call me "Coach Prime."

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.234
-"Coach Prime."
-Yeah, like --

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.901
-Yeah, I'm gonna call you
"Coach Prime."

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.300
It's back with new episodes.
Congratulations on that.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.734
-Thank you.
-Pretty historic season,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.000
by the way.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.200
-It's the first time
in Jackson State history,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.434
I want to say, that the team
won 11 games in a season.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:57.868
-Yes.
-Also want to -- yeah.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's -- that's you.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:03.868
And two of your sons
play on the team.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:04.834
-Yes.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:05.968
-Do they get any
special treatment?

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.300
-None whatsoever.
First of all,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.167
they may get it harder
than the other kids.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.467
If you know which kids
are my son,

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:15.033
other than the way they look,
I'm not doing my job coaching.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.367
I'm tough.
I'm disciplined.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:21.200
I'm tenacious on the kids.
But I want them to be smart,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.434
tough, fast, disciplined,
with character.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:24.934
And I gotta have that.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.000
If I don't have it,
you're not playing for us.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.367
I demand that.
-Yeah, you do.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.067
That's good. That's why --
That's why you win.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.701
I love this.
I love the show.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.667
But do the kid know that
not only did you

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:39.267
play the Super Bowl, you also
played in the World Series?

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.767
-The kids that play for me?
-Yeah.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.567
-Yeah, they kind of --

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.501
Trust me,
when we travel somewhere,

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.267
there's police escorts.
It's --

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.767
We do it big, so they kind of
know who their coach is.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.300
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.834
-They gotta know they coach
is a little different.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:54.701
He's cut a little different.
-Do they know that

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:57.100
their coach also had, like,
a brief rap career?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.434
-They know they coach had hits.
Yeah, hits.

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:02.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:03.801
-Hitss.
-Hitss.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.968
-Hits-suh.
-Yeah, you add an extra S --

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.467
the hitss, yeah, yeah.
-Hits-suh.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.467
-I bought this CD.
-You should've.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.534
-I did.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:11.534
-You should've.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.033
-This is
"Prime Time Deion Sanders."

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.701
-Look at you, man.
Come on.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:20.167
-[ Laughing ]
"Must be the Money" was my jam.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.434
-"Must be the Money"
was the one.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:22.734
-That was the jam right there.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.167
Actually, we have a little bit
of the music video.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.133
-Uh-oh.
-Just to remind you.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.200
-Oh, Lord.
-Yeah. Take a look.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.067
♪ Flashing lights
on the dance floor ♪

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:35.834
♪ The DJ says my name
as I make my intro ♪

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:36.834
♪ Must be the money ♪

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.801
-♪ Must be the money ♪

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.501
-♪ I got so much jewels ♪
♪ Must be the money ♪

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.367
-♪ Must be the money ♪

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.934
-Yeah, that is "Prime Time"!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.734
That's my man.
-I thank God.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.734
God allowed me
to live out all my dreams.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:53.567
And you got to understand,
every athlete wants to be

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.801
an entertainer,
and every entertainer

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.267
wants to be somewhat
of an athlete.

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.868
-Exactly.
-And I got to live out my dream.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.400
I'm -- I was excited.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.868
I still have hits
in me left, though.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.300
-You -- You have more hitss.
-Yes-suh.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.567
-Yeah, exactly, hits-suh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.334
Your just finished
your full season

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:11.601
at Jackson State,
which is a HBCU.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.133
-Yes.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.534
-What made you
take that coaching job?

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:16.934
-Why not?
Why not?

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:21.000
It was a tremendous opportunity
to advance equality,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.667
to allow people
to understand there is a --

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.200
not just a devastation,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.734
that it's a turbulent time
in HBCU sports.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.834
And I just wanted to bring a --
shed light, bring equality,

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:35.033
bring a spotlight
on the programs.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.200
And that's what we've
accomplished at Jackson State.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.200
-Yeah, you've done that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.100
It's amazing.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.634
You're also having
the NFL look at players?

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:49.734
-Yeah, well,
we already had an NFL combine.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:52.167
We have the NFL pro day
on our campus,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.501
which is going
to now track NFL scouts.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.334
They've come from the --

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.968
Dozens of scouts has come
to our practices now.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.968
All of the HBCUs, we're getting
better quality of players.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.968
Now, kids coming out
of high school,

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.234
they're not saying no, and the
HBCUs are recruiting them now.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.367
Once upon a time, they didn't
think they could get them.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.901
But now they're saying,
"You know what?

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.234
We're going after
that four-star,

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:14.567
we're going after
that five-star."

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.467
We just happened to get
the best kid in the country,

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.000
the number-one recruit,
period, last season.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.534
[ Applause ]

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:21.667
-Period.
-Period.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:26.167
-Our buddy -- our buddy Shaq --
we love him.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.467
He was talking about you
the other day.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.934
And he said that he thinks
that you should maybe be

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.467
the coach of the Dallas Cowboys.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.601
-I love Jerry Jones,
I love the Cowboys,

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.334
but I cannot coach pros.
I have a problem

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.834
with a professional athlete
not doing his job

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.400
and he's getting
handsomely paid.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.634
I don't have
any toleration for that.

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.334
There's some out there
working their butts off,

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:48.367
but there's plenty out there
that just don't get it.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.434
And I would fight.

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:50.901
I would fight every day,
as a coach.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:52.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.834
I couldn't do it.
I'm old school.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.601
-You're old school, yeah.
-I'm old school, man.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:58.234
You know, we -- you made it
this far from your work ethic.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:00.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it -- it would be tough.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.000
-Yeah, because you see
these kids, they -- they want --

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.834
they want to play.
They want to play the game.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.100
-Yes. The college kids,
they want to play.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.067
-Exactly.
-Yes.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.934
-That's right.
There's also --

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:10.901
What do you think about the --
the thing that's been coming up

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.868
that there's not enough
Black coaches in the NFL?

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.300
-That's true.
-Yeah.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.534
-But the solvency of the problem
is where everyone is deferred.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.067
You can't make a billionaire do

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:21.467
what a billionaire
don't want to do.

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:23.601
You can't make --
you hire a housekeeper

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.734
you don't want to hire.
To solve -- bring solvency

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:29.133
to this problem,
I think we should demand

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.767
that there are three to four
expansion teams,

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:37.167
and you give those teams
to an ethnic group.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.567
Then you see how it --
see how it falls.

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:42.167
See how it plays out, as owners.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:44.400
We need three Black owners,
and let's see how it plays out.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.501
[ Applause ]

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:50.000
-I like that.
-I like it, too.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.734
-Let's talk about "Coach Prime."

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.000
This follows the ups and downs
of the season.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.734
Can you talk about what people
are gonna see this season?

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:57.968
-It's gonna be phenomenal.
Dana Beers is a producer.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:05:59.267
"Dana Beers is a producer" --

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:00.667
that sounded funny
coming out my mouth.

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:03.400
"Dana Beers is a producer."
He's phenomenal.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.634
You're gonna see trials,
tribulations,

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.167
especially with myself
personally.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.634
You're gonna see
these kids triumph.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:13.267
You're gonna see devastation,
tribulations, and trials,

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:16.167
and situations that they
overcome adversity.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.567
But you're gonna see a real
inside look of how we get down.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.434
And we don't sugarcoat anything.
-You don't.

00:06:21.434 --> 00:06:23.033
-No, you're gonna see the truth.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:25.067
Do you remember those moments?
I mean, I know

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:26.767
what happened to you,
but also, I mean,

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:28.667
those moments where you go,
like, "I can't do it"?

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:31.133
-I never said I can't do it.
That's not in my vocabulary,

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:32.367
"I can't do it."
-Never?

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.434
-No, I'm the
Little Engine That Could.

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:34.567
I was on that train.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:37.334
I said, "I think I can,
I think I can."

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:38.334
-Yeah.
-"I think I can."

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.801
-"I think I can."
-"I think I can."

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:41.267
-"I think I can.
I know I can."

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.667
-"I know I can."
There you go.

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:44.868
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's a peek at this season

00:06:44.868 --> 00:06:46.901
of "Coach Prime."
Take a look.

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:51.601
-I'm tired of us just not living
up to our fullest potential.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:55.200
Fellas, I'm tired.
And it's making me weary.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.133
I didn't lose my voice
from yelling.

00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:59.901
I lose my voice because it's
a tactic of the enemy

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.667
to try to mess with my mobility
and my voice,

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:07.300
because my voice changes things.
And I'm tired.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:10.267
I'm gonna continue to fight,
though, in my weariness.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.801
I'm gonna continue to believe,

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.300
even though nobody else
believes.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.667
I'm gonna continue to walk even
if I have to shoot myself up.

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:19.434
But each and every one of y'all
give me strength, man.

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:22.501
Y'all give me purpose.
Y'all keep me going.

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:26.000
Y'all give me hope.
Y'all make me believe.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.067
And y'all could do that today.

00:07:28.067 --> 00:07:29.667
Because I'm not gonna
lie to you -- I'm tired.

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:32.367
If you don't do
nothing else today,

00:07:32.367 --> 00:07:35.734
give me some strength,
because I'm tired.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:38.968
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:44.334
-Now, right when I end,
I look away, and I say,

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:45.834
"Now give me my theme music,"

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:49.000
and that's when it comes on,
and the kids go crazy, man.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.567
-You know how to do it.
-They love it.

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:52.767
-That's Deion Sanders,
everybody.

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:54.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Coach Prime"

00:07:54.834 --> 00:07:57.801
on all Barstool Sports
digital channels.

